description:
The parity test explicitly checks only 'field name presence — not type-based'. It cannot detect:
(a) integer-vs-fractional mismatches (the integer-column finding);
(b) nullability (TS optional vs PG NOT NULL + sanitizeRow, e.g. indication; null-after-pull);
(c) CHECK lists vs TS unions vs backup zod unions (the potassium/PRN backup drift);
(d) the Dexie table list itself, which is a hard-coded TABLE_TO_INTERFACE map never cross-checked against db.ts stores or TABLE_PUSH_ORDER;
(e) FK deletion order.
The real-Postgres integration test covers ""→NULL only for nullable columns (source, note, groupId), never for a NOT NULL column. The wipe, cleanup and account-delete tests mock the DB.

